# RopeTool.Mod's own sub clamps a start past the end to the empty rope
# (0-based start=100); rope_tool's slice S LOW HIGH uses LOW = Length
# (Source) + 1 = 12 (the one valid "past the literal end" position,
# matching Ropes.Slice's own Null_Rope-not-an-error boundary when
# High < Low -- see PLAN.md's "Access and slicing") with HIGH < LOW, so
# this is still an empty rope, printed as a blank output line, same
# outcome as the original for a differently-chosen boundary value (100
# itself would raise Index_Error here -- see PLAN.md's "Modification"
# section on why Ropes.Mod's permissive clamping was not carried over
# wholesale).
program rope_tool
arg slice
arg hello world
arg 12
arg 11
status 0
output

